# DAMA-CRM Project Rules

## 1. Permanent Logo Assets Rule
- The official and immutable logos of DAMA-CRM are in `client/public/assets/logos/`:
  - `dama-symbol-dark.png`
  - `dama-symbol-white.png`
  - `dama-symbol-color.png`
  - `dama-logo-dark.png`
  - `dama-logo-white.png`
  - `dama-logo-color.png`
  - `dama-logo-black.png`
  - `dama-logo-vertical-dark.png`
  - `dama-logo-vertical-white.png`
  - `sample-company-logo.svg`
- NEVER delete, modify, or replace these logos. Always use these PNG files for branding.

## 2. Light Mode Theme Scale
- Light mode MUST always use a comfortable grayscale / slate scale (`bg-slate-100/90` / `#F1F5F9`) instead of blinding pure white backgrounds.

## 3. Centered Popups and Modals
- All popups, dialogs, and modals (Language modal, Onboarding wizard, Time tracking / Clock-in / Harvest Widget, User Profile, Notifications) MUST be centered in the screen (`fixed inset-0 flex items-center justify-center p-4 m-auto`), NEVER positioned at the top of the screen.

## 4. No "God Mode" or "Master Tenant" Jargon in UI
- NEVER display "God Mode", "Master Tenant", "Salir a Master", or "God Admin" in visible user interfaces, badges, or buttons. Keep all terminology corporate and clean (e.g., "Primary Company", "Administrator", "Settings").

## 5. Harvest-Style Persistent Time Tracking
- Workday and task time tracking (`ClockWidget.tsx`, `time-tracking.controller.ts`) MUST operate on server-side UTC timestamps (`clockIn`, `lastResumedAt`, `accumulatedSeconds`).
- Time tracking MUST persist across browser close, tab close, and computer reboot without losing a second.
- Support Harvest features: Project & Task selection, Billable toggle, Notes, Pause/Resume, Task switching with automatic WorkLog creation.

## 6. 100% Idempotent Migrations
- All SQL migrations (`server/prisma/migrations/`) must be strictly idempotent using `IF NOT EXISTS` and safe `DO $$ BEGIN ... END $$;` constraint blocks.

## 7. Chrome and Firefox Browser Extensions
- The `extension/` directory houses companion extensions for Google Chrome (MV3) and Mozilla Firefox (MV2/Gecko) providing live time tracking, badge countdown, and task management.
